# Integrality of Δ(q)/Δ(q^ℓ) over ℚ[j]

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.isIntegral_adjoin_jq_modularUnitSeries`
(`b1bdf829-d1bb-5bb1-9a0a-29db5f98a3e4`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `2f81c8b9-01d9-5257-b99b-0956ff264f65`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $\ell$ be a prime. Consider the field of formal Laurent series $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ (Lean
`LaurentSeries ℚ`) and in it the two elements built as follows:
[`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) is $q^{-1}$ times the power series `jNumQ`, the
image under $\mathbb{Z}\to\mathbb{Q}$ of the integral power series `jNum`, so that `jq` is the
$q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$; and [`ModularCurve.modularUnitSeries
ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_ModularUnit.html#L127) is the product of
[`ModularCurve.deltaSeries`](def/ModularCurve_ModularUnit.html#L107), namely $q$ times the rational
power series `dedekindEtaUnitQ`, with the inverse of [`ModularCurve.deltaSeriesN
ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_ModularUnit.html#L119), the series obtained from
[`ModularCurve.deltaSeries`](def/ModularCurve_ModularUnit.html#L107) by the substitution $q \mapsto
q^{\ell}$ (Lean `qExpand ℚ ℓ`). Thus [`ModularCurve.modularUnitSeries
ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_ModularUnit.html#L127) is the formal Laurent expansion of
$\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^{\ell})$. The assertion is that this element is integral over the
$\mathbb{Q}$-subalgebra $\mathbb{Q}[\,$`jq`$\,]$ of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by `jq`, that is, it
is a root of a monic polynomial all of whose coefficients are polynomials in `jq` with rational
coefficients.

This is the integrality over $\mathbb{Q}[j]$ of Ogg's modular unit $u_\ell =
\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^{\ell})$ on $X_0(\ell)$, the formal-series form of the statement that $u_\ell$ is
a modular function for $\Gamma_0(\ell)$ holomorphic away from the cusps. It is used, together with
the corresponding statement for $u_\ell^{-1}$, in the analysis of places of the function field of
$X_0(\ell)$ and of specialisations at which $j$ is integral, where it forces $u_\ell$ to have order
zero at every such place.

